ly.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb0ae539-5348-5a2c-b226-c009ce6d6094" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 7"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023e8ca5-d704-5d99-b064-aeb77c93d254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432700} {:answer/id #uuid "2022291e-1db1-5780-8ab9-edc149d22ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II  and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432709} {:answer/id #uuid "2e82d512-84f1-533e-a037-9f343f12a528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432714} {:answer/id #uuid "dc070f7d-66ad-5425-aa52-08341f6869d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432757} {:answer/id #uuid "f8032825-bbee-58b1-b581-15121282664c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I  and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc070f7d-66ad-5425-aa52-08341f6869d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432757} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad4a570e-3aef-54f0-a307-e26d4ea86c53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6daa78eb-7b75-5f11-9d14-72a95f4ad0c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-223454" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $434$\n\nII. $785$\n\nIII. $587$" :question/worked-solution "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $434,$ we have that \n\n$$\n43-2(4)=43-8=35\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $434$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $785,$ we have that \n\n$$\n78-2(5)=78-10=68\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $785$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $587,$ we have that \n\n$$\n58-2(7)=58-14=44\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $587$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0120a1f8-aa48-5ed0-8305-31cbb2b1f611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432699} {:answer/id #uuid "444908dd-fb48-51a9-b264-374c7d885080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432718} {:answer/id #uuid "53497952-583e-5109-a21b-c6bd9897e804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432723} {:answer/id #uuid "aebf6a52-e58b-5a25-b8d3-5595904827e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432741} {:answer/id #uuid "cd965191-d33a-5755-b2e3-4b0b273f31d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53497952-583e-5109-a21b-c6bd9897e804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432723} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9354ff-3d30-5d4e-a8f1-a17d95295904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d8254ce-5d00-53a5-a718-295062329804" :question/math-academy-id "q-85144" :question/problem "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $173\\,◻32\\,338$ divisible by $9?$\n\nI. $4$\n\nII. $6$\n\nIII. $9$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\nFor the number $173\\,◻32\\,338\\,$ the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n1+7+3+◻+3+2+3+3+8=30+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits that could be inserted into the blank.\n\n- If we insert $4$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $30+4=34,$ which is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- If we insert $6$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $30+6=36,$ which is divisible by $9.$\n\n- If we insert $9$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $30+9=39,$ which is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b483f9f7-47a9-5725-b1f1-fe0ea39a7e96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 6"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a2752c1-636c-52a6-a6d4-6d9b59cbf421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432713} {:answer/id #uuid "4d83589b-d420-59c9-bbed-964e663c6b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432720} {:answer/id #uuid "8dac666f-2957-5b5a-bf69-321c0d67de2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432732} {:answer/id #uuid "cd42dba0-3bec-5cb3-9e1f-c94b56e7c76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432751} {:answer/id #uuid "f0877883-a791-5d0e-bd93-e8b6c16fdb44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd42dba0-3bec-5cb3-9e1f-c94b56e7c76a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432751} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3d65056-5e8f-5f44-8d4d-595ca231767e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91c8241d-8043-5a59-abeb-68e020936dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-132408" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $345\\,989\\,191$\n\nII. $55\\,355\\,676$\n\nIII. $137\\,252\\,124$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $345\\,989\\,191$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $55\\,355\\,676$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n5+5+3+5+5+6+7+6=42\n$$\n\nSo, $55\\,355\\,676$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $137\\,252\\,124$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+3+7+2+5+2+1+2+4=27\n$$\n\nSo, $137\\,252\\,124$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb0ae539-5348-5a2c-b226-c009ce6d6094" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 7"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c90b2bd-a16e-537c-aa1a-b49d1b1aa9f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432724} {:answer/id #uuid "69d77dac-58f7-5252-9e21-125e39d4033b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432727} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d0a1e6-9bc7-54e5-adb0-ec9f8743d848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432740} {:answer/id #uuid "b11e3ef3-de26-5e2b-a700-7f2ecb279329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432744} {:answer/id #uuid "d8eb41db-fc65-5243-aa64-63b69ecf8947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5d0a1e6-9bc7-54e5-adb0-ec9f8743d848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432740} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4c20e9-b428-5717-aa65-b028512ceffa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "951452dc-b5fb-50d7-8d4f-8b1233b43cf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-223369" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $447$\n\nII. $406$\n\nIII. $847$" :question/worked-solution "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $447,$ we have that \n\n$$\n44-2(7)=44-14=30\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $447$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $406,$ we have that \n\n$$\n40-2(6)=40-12=28\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $406$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $847,$ we have that \n\n$$\n84-2(7)=84-14=70\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $847$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b483f9f7-47a9-5725-b1f1-fe0ea39a7e96" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 6"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03716efb-8dd0-5692-a7ad-ddc54290f97c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432702} {:answer/id #uuid "c7079a82-b92a-5d2b-9c94-e0b3d56ba29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432750} {:answer/id #uuid "d53103cc-e21c-5a43-a029-4914bb36a519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432753} {:answer/id #uuid "d86b4192-f97c-51d0-8a92-2939d373fe1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432755} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf7965c-4e93-5f39-a663-6a32dce50c9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03716efb-8dd0-5692-a7ad-ddc54290f97c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432702} :answer-field/id #uuid "008ba33f-0dbe-5e5d-81fc-18953e1cddb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a49592c2-4649-5980-ab80-d5418f7e763f" :question/math-academy-id "q-85422" :question/problem "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $114\\,040\\,32◻$ divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $0$\n\nII. $5$\n\nIII. $6$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$ Remember that to determine whether a number is divisible by $3,$ we check whether the sum of the digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the given number, the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n1+1+4+0+4+0+3+2+◻=15+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits we can substitute into the blank.\n\n- If we substitute $0$ into the blank, we get $114\\,040\\,320,$ which is divisible by $2.$ The sum of the digits is $15+0=15,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\n- If we substitute $5$ into the blank, we get $114\\,040\\,325,$ which is not divisible by $2.$ So, the number is *not* divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- If we substitute $6$ into the blank, we get $114\\,040\\,326,$ which is divisible by $2.$ The sum of the digits is $15+6=21,$ which is divisible by $3,$ so the number is also divisible by $3.$ Therefore, the number is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17fae707-234b-5507-93c9-8b38a5d9f1bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432707} {:answer/id #uuid "19e13b1c-16f5-5fc8-a671-833b5709b8d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432708} {:answer/id #uuid "af45d2a1-5a3b-5c3e-9120-03abfd5ec846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432743} {:answer/id #uuid "bad2a1ab-31c5-5027-a0be-787091378f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432745} {:answer/id #uuid "d6394eaa-ebbb-50b8-bf10-523ea6eac961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6394eaa-ebbb-50b8-bf10-523ea6eac961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432754} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dcd5f48-4894-5201-9b6d-2e2eb2a453bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9669189-f542-5fc7-9dce-62db6de9555d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132386" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $3?$\n\nI. $935\\,784$\n\nII. $7\\,391\\,123$\n\nIII. $12\\,144\\,801$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $935\\,784$ is\n\n$$\n9+3+5+7+8+4=36,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So, $935\\,784$ is divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $7\\,391\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+9+1+1+2+3=26,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $3.$ So, $7\\,391\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $12\\,144\\,801$ is\n\n$$\n1+2+1+4+4+8+0+1=21,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $3.$ So,  $12\\,144\\,801$ is divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8fa39c-a982-569a-b2e0-833c51259711" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 3 or 9"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121e7df8-8657-5dcb-a92f-506287be02dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432705} {:answer/id #uuid "6999ccbb-0da9-56ee-9ed1-618bb6718054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432726} {:answer/id #uuid "89c0a663-188b-568b-84c7-12a167670681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432731} {:answer/id #uuid "c423a550-f52a-5b4e-b53b-5d4f5453fe48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432749} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d8ff3d-ef9d-5ac4-8135-04c1399c5e26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c423a550-f52a-5b4e-b53b-5d4f5453fe48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432749} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd1116a6-2d8a-5e7c-bbb8-69191fa04e08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432780}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2757e05-6aab-58ae-aed8-77516507381e" :question/math-academy-id "q-132392" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $9?$\n\nI. $34\\,154\\,119$\n\nII. $9\\,173\\,589$\n\nIII. $733\\,123$" :question/worked-solution "A number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $34\\,154\\,119$ is\n\n$$\n3+4+1+5+4+1+1+9=28,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $34\\,154\\,119$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $9\\,173\\,589$ is\n\n$$\n9+1+7+3+5+8+9=42,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $9\\,173\\,589$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $733\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+3+1+2+3=19,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $733\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb0ae539-5348-5a2c-b226-c009ce6d6094" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 7"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d82c8ca-e2a0-5442-acfc-6cf1aba5809b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432704} {:answer/id #uuid "2a0c050b-dbdf-51df-b498-80916aea50b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432712} {:answer/id #uuid "32d2feef-0a50-5be6-8be0-cc007b6c7465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432715} {:answer/id #uuid "50fc2e21-2e60-5152-8ded-84b094c83b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432722} {:answer/id #uuid "aec18c88-4572-5f31-bf18-6f1c2e43c5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432742}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aec18c88-4572-5f31-bf18-6f1c2e43c5c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432742} :answer-field/id #uuid "d41a4fb2-3b50-5439-ab7b-d9726d39fc08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0e5ee54-f96c-54ab-8de5-f272c76ac6c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-223365" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $448$\n\nII. $352$\n\nIII. $217$" :question/worked-solution "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $448,$ we have that \n\n$$\n44-2(8)=44-16=28\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $448$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $352,$ we have that \n\n$$\n35-2(2)=35-4=31\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $352$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $217,$ we have that \n\n$$\n21-2(7)=21-14=7\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $217$ is divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb0ae539-5348-5a2c-b226-c009ce6d6094" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Number Is Divisible by 7"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "031e87af-b7df-5caa-98ff-dd4bdf5b2596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432701} {:answer/id #uuid "4a0625b5-89d4-5e5f-9799-0edb2744330c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432719} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c3fe5c-f2c3-50ce-8bd4-e2d9ace1ee05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432737} {:answer/id #uuid "a4cbcf82-d526-53da-9a10-140590b0bd4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432739} {:answer/id #uuid "ed58acbc-01e1-5d2e-8ccf-549196fdfa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed58acbc-01e1-5d2e-8ccf-549196fdfa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432762} :answer-field/id #uuid "3188a9e7-7b59-59ac-8edf-b18ab2c46193" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fdf659d7-2ff6-5274-9913-97ffa0cf4e09" :question/math-academy-id "q-223456" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $476$\n\nII. $732$\n\nIII. $423$" :question/worked-solution "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $476,$ we have that \n\n$$\n47-2(6)=47-12=35\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $476$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $732,$ we have that \n\n$$\n73-2(2)=73-4=69\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $732$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $423,$ we have that \n\n$$\n42-2(3)=42-6=36\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $423$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5594b522-b05d-56b3-b912-961b140aeac9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$V$ and $W$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433126} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea03761-fa6e-5cb3-aed6-0f335e32102b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433130} {:answer/id #uuid "8f442901-c3b7-5866-82d6-1cf54562946a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U$ and $V$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433131} {:answer/id #uuid "902457a9-b694-5355-8804-d4836495776f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433132} {:answer/id #uuid "b4b5b8f0-d7c4-56e8-91b3-1eb6a0e8b98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ea03761-fa6e-5cb3-aed6-0f335e32102b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433130} :answer-field/id #uuid "88d26e7d-7cf7-53de-a739-9d6548330c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433144}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cc85c8f-2fc1-51b5-90b3-b4c40aaa9ac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-40288" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nI. $U=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nII. $V=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nIII. $W=\\{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n$\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}\\},$ \n$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\},$ and \n$\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}\\},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The set $U$ cannot be orthogonal since it contains  $3$ vectors from ${R}^{2}$ (in which we can have an orthogonal set with at most 2 non-zero vectors). Therefore, $U$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=0+10=10\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=12+3-1=14\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"None of the listed\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e486175-d93e-59a1-beee-b5e17fb3fe9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$V$ and $W$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433123} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1dfe6a-46a2-5b7b-b9a2-2e4f0b6a6290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433128} {:answer/id #uuid "99a6a3de-f047-5ffa-a17f-a1fea25b4278" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433134} {:answer/id #uuid "b440af9e-0d7a-5e18-bcec-b34eee928e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$V$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433138} {:answer/id #uuid "c833776b-5d21-59ee-8ccb-29989a9b9e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$U$ and $W$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b440af9e-0d7a-5e18-bcec-b34eee928e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$V$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433138} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c41282-b496-53fd-b601-ecca0a4b4a0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f013658-0e98-56e3-b0df-e2d26e152fca" :question/math-academy-id "q-140479" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nI. $U=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nII. $V=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nIII. $W=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n$\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2}\\},$ \n$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\},$ and \n$\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{2}\\},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0,\\,{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0,\\,{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=-3+0-2+2=-3\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=4-4=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=2+0-4+2=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0+6-4-2=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $V$ is orthogonal.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=2+2+4=8\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$V$ only\"."}]}
